('use_of_english_0271', 'Use of English', 'Appropriate word choice', 'Word Choice in Context', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "kxwnre"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 1, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "B", "explanation": "Dangerous contradicts the stated reason (amusing) and instead fits a context of risk or threat.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "Sad is the opposite emotional tone to amusing, an error a student might make by rushing past the reason clause.", "misconceptionId": "rushed_under_pressure"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "Libellous relates to damaging false statements, a legal concept unrelated to something being amusing.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2002, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Fill each gap with the most appropriate option from the lists provided.

