('use_of_english_0274', 'Use of English', 'Consonants', 'Consonant Sounds', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "3p5hul"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "The ''s'' sound (spelled ''ce'') in grace represents /s/, not /z/, matching the letter shape rather than the actual pronunciation.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "Rice ends in the /s/ sound, easily confused with rise due to their similar spelling, but the sounds differ.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "The initial ''s'' in sink is /s/, an easy default choice since ''s'' most commonly represents /s/ rather than /z/.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2002, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that has the same consonant sound as the one represented by the underlined letter(s).

